# Checked out LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says. bash reads a
# CR as part of the last word on a line, so a Windows checkout of a script or a
# .conf fails in ways that look like the code is wrong rather than the file.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
.runbranch  text eol=lf
*.go        text eol=lf
*.swift     text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
